  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8231754",
      "title": "Working with Effect Dependencies & useCallback",
      "sourceHash": "d64dc05c555a8362a759a40fe85fae4bcd0a2fbf90ff0d8aba5a4dc4bb9dcfb0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "Now to understand what's wrong here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "let's first of all add a couple of console log statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "here in QuestionTimer.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "and I'll add one right in this effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 14.163,
          "en": "where I set my timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 19.053,
          "en": "Here I'll basically say SETTING TIMEOUT,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 23.25,
          "en": "and I'll copy that to the second useEffect call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.25,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "where I set my interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 28.203,
          "en": "and therefore I'll say SETTING INTERVAL here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "Now one thing you'll notice if you save that and reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "and open the console here is that you get those logs twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "but that's only happening because we're in StrictMode here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "in the main JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "the whole app is wrapped in StrictMode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 50.88,
          "en": "and that StrictMode actually calls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.88,
          "end": 53.76,
          "en": "every component function twice behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.76,
          "end": 57.363,
          "en": "since this can help you catch certain issues.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "But you'll also notice if you reload again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 66.26,
          "en": "that as this timer expires, nothing happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 71.96000000000001,
          "en": "but then after a while a new timer is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 74.493,
          "en": "but not a new interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "There we still only have the old logs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "But this timer keeps getting a reset,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 83.97,
          "en": "as you can tell by this number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 87.36,
          "en": "in front of SETTING TIMEOUT, which is incrementing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 90.15299999999999,
          "en": "which changed to two and now to three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.23,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "So clearly this effect function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 97.32300000000001,
          "en": "keeps on getting executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "And that is weird because this QuestionTimer component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 106.65,
          "en": "is rendered once, here, when that quiz is being rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 109.89,
          "en": "but it's not getting recreated thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.89,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "Sure, the quiz component rerenders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 116.91,
          "en": "whenever an answer is selected, but this component instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.91,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "of the question timer does not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "It was part of the old JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 125.73,
          "en": "It is part of the new JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "So in theory, this effect function shouldn't execute again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 131.85,
          "en": "and for example, this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.85,
          "end": 135.57,
          "en": "where the interval is set does not execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "As you see in the log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 139.77,
          "en": "it's just the timeout effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.77,
          "end": 142.71,
          "en": "that was executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.71,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "So the fact that this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "keeps on getting executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 150.573,
          "en": "must be related to our dependencies here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "Now one dependency is the timeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 156.51,
          "en": "and that value never changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.51,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "So that should not trigger the effect function to run again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 161.79,
          "en": "because as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 164.55,
          "en": "the effect function is executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.55,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "if the surrounding component function executes again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.79,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "and the dependency values changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 174.32999999999998,
          "en": "and for a timeout that will definitely not be the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.32999999999998,
          "end": 177.037,
          "en": "it is always 10,000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.14,
          "end": 181.92,
          "en": "So it must be this function that changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.92,
          "end": 184.833,
          "en": "That's the only possible explanation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.7,
          "end": 189.21,
          "en": "And indeed this is what's happening here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.21,
          "end": 193.02,
          "en": "because as you also learned in the previous section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.02,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "functions in JavaScript are values, they are objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 200.55,
          "en": "And when a function is created like here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.55,
          "end": 203.13,
          "en": "when this JSX code is evaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.13,
          "end": 207.24,
          "en": "it is a new object in memory that's being created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.24,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "And even if it contains the same logic and code as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 214.263,
          "en": "it's still technically a new value in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.57999999999998,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "So every time this JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 220.77,
          "en": "in this quiz component gets reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.77,
          "end": 222.963,
          "en": "a new function gets created here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 227.49,
          "en": "And this JSX code gets reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.49,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "whenever the state in this quiz component is updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 233.703,
          "en": "which happens when the user picks an answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.63,
          "end": 237.84,
          "en": "Now, to work around that we have to do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.84,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "which you learned in the last section as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "We have to use another special hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 247.92,
          "en": "which ensures that functions don't get recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.92,
          "end": 252.48,
          "en": "unless they need because their dependencies changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.48,
          "end": 255.363,
          "en": "We need to use the useCallback hook here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 257.16,
          "end": 260.64300000000003,
          "en": "We need to use it and wrap this function with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 265.02,
          "en": "Now to not violate any rules of hooks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 265.02,
          "end": 267.72,
          "en": "and use this hook in this nested code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.72,
          "end": 271,
          "en": "I will actually go up here below handleSelectAnswer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.86,
          "end": 276.10699999999997,
          "en": "and add a new constant that could be called handleSkipAnswer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 278.22,
          "end": 281.793,
          "en": "because that's in the end what happens if the timer expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 287.92,
          "en": "And here I'll then store the return value of useCallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.99,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "and I'll then wrap this function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 296.82,
          "en": "which I had down here, this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 296.82,
          "end": 297.93,
          "en": "I'll cut it from here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 297.93,
          "end": 301.473,
          "en": "and wrap it with useCallback like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 306.191,
          "en": "And then, as you learned in the previous section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 306.191,
          "end": 309.24,
          "en": "useCallback also needs a dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 309.24,
          "end": 312.633,
          "en": "that lists all dependencies that might be used in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 314.4,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "Now, in here I am indeed using a dependency.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 321.273,
          "en": "I am indeed using the handleSelectAnswer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 322.86,
          "end": 325.05,
          "en": "So technically we should add that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 325.05,
          "end": 328.02,
          "en": "as a dependency here in this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 328.02,
          "end": 330.84,
          "en": "because this is a value created here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.84,
          "end": 332.55,
          "en": "in this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 332.55,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "which could depend on props and state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 338.97,
          "en": "So therefore, indirectly, this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 338.97,
          "end": 342.825,
          "en": "depends on props and state, and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.825,
          "end": 346.56,
          "en": "we should also use useCallback here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 346.56,
          "end": 348.25,
          "en": "and create handleSelectAnswer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 349.74,
          "end": 354.74,
          "en": "by wrapping this function here with useCallback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 357.12,
          "end": 360.603,
          "en": "and there we also have to add our list of dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 366.06,
          "en": "But here we now don't have to add anything to that list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 366.06,
          "end": 369.87,
          "en": "because in this handleSelectAnswer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 369.87,
          "end": 373.2,
          "en": "we are not using any state or props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 373.2,
          "end": 378.2,
          "en": "and also not any other values that depend on state or props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 379.08,
          "end": 381.42,
          "en": "A state updating functions like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 383.1,
          "en": "don't have to be added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 383.1,
          "end": 386.493,
          "en": "because React will guarantee that they never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 388.83,
          "end": 390.75,
          "en": "Well, and with all that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 390.75,
          "end": 394.89,
          "en": "we now have functions that are not recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 394.89,
          "end": 398.04,
          "en": "just because the surrounding component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 398.04,
          "end": 402.36,
          "en": "was executed again, and therefore it's now handleSkipAnswer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 402.36,
          "end": 404.85,
          "en": "which I pass to on timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 404.85,
          "end": 408.202,
          "en": "And as I do that, if I reload, you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.202,
          "end": 412.08,
          "en": "that the timeout and interval is set initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 412.08,
          "end": 413.82,
          "en": "but not thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 413.82,
          "end": 415.994,
          "en": "As we move to a new question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 415.994,
          "end": 419.043,
          "en": "the timeout is now not set again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 420.06,
          "end": 424.41,
          "en": "Now we still have that weird pause after the timer expired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 424.41,
          "end": 428.25,
          "en": "where we're not moving on to the next answer instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 428.25,
          "end": 429.9,
          "en": "or to the next question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 429.9,
          "end": 432.903,
          "en": "but that's something we'll fix in the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}